second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is the primary instrument played by Allah Rakha?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 170, \"text\": \"Alla Rakha Ustad Allarakha Qureshi (29 April 1919 – 3 February 2000), popularly known as Alla Rakha, was an Indian tabla player specialized in Hindustani Classical music.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d00\", \"start\": 171, \"end\": 230, \"text\": \"He was a frequent accompanist of sitar player Ravi Shankar.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d00\", \"start\": 231, \"end\": 297, \"text\": \"Allah Rakha was born in Ghagwal, Jammu and Kashmir, British India.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d00\", \"start\": 298, \"end\": 326, \"text\": \"His mother tongue was Dogri.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d00\", \"start\": 327, \"end\": 447, \"text\": \"He became fascinated with the sound and rhythm of the tabla at the age of 12, while staying with his uncle in Gurdaspur.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d00\", \"start\": 448, \"end\": 596, \"text\": \"Finding little chances for grooming and appreciation, the determined young lad ran away from home, became a disciple of tabla began studying it with\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 116, \"text\": \"'' sitar ) the playable strings are strung in this fashion : Chikari strings : Sa ( high ) , Sa ( middle ) , and Pa.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d01\", \"start\": 117, \"end\": 170, \"text\": \"Kharaj ( bass ) strings : Sa ( low ) and Pa ( low ) .\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d01\", \"start\": 171, \"end\": 205, \"text\": \"Jod and baaj strings , Sa and Ma .\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d01\", \"start\": 206, \"end\": 338, \"text\": \"There is a lot of stylistic variance within these tunings , and like most Indian stringed instruments , there is no default tuning .\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d01\", \"start\": 339, \"end\": 438, \"text\": \"Mostly , tunings vary by schools of teaching ( gharana ) and the piece that is meant to be played .\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d01\", \"start\": 439, \"end\": 453, \"text\": \"Playing [ edit\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0057-f68ce0bb3608:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Alla Rakha\", \"scope\": \"primary instrument\", \"claim\": \"Alla Rakha was an Indian tabla player specialized in Hindustani Classical music.\", \"answer\": \"tabla\", \"quote\": \"Alla Rakha Ustad Allarakha Qureshi (29 April 1919 – 3 February 2000), popularly known as Alla Rakha, was an Indian tabla player specialized in Hindustani Classical music.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}], \"R5_answers\": [\"tabla\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"tabla\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
